Modified by OpenResearchTools for BashKitten on 23 September 2026:
- Expose one JSON query-or-URL command, using DDGS for search, and a normally
  discovered Pi skill with adapted search-then-read guidance.
- Run with packaged native Linux/Termux Python dependencies and private,
  persistent output paths. Keep the search helper separate from stock Pi.
- Save the complete extracted Markdown before returning a 16,000-character
  inline preview and the full file path. Remove hard download-size, page-count
  and extraction-count caps; preserve explicit cancellation and read errors.
- Retain the PDF reader and its text/layout fallback, always attempt Markdown
  conversion, and omit unrelated RAG ingestion and image tools.
- Integrate the separately attributed GitHub repository and YouTube transcript
  readers into the same command. SearXNG and the Unsloth Studio application
  itself are not included.

